{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Acid reflux happens when stomach contents flow back into the esophagus, often due to the lower esophageal sphincter (LES) not closing properly. The underlying reasons can be surprising:\n\n**Why Acid Reflux Happens**\n- **Low Stomach Acid:** Contrary to popular belief, acid reflux is often caused by too little stomach acid, not too much. Low acid impairs digestion and can cause the LES to relax, allowing acid to escape upward.\n- **Aging & Lifestyle:** Stomach acid production naturally decreases with age. Stress, poor diet (especially refined sugars), certain medications, and even drinking too much water with meals can further reduce acid levels.\n- **Other Triggers:** Food allergies, candida overgrowth, and mineral/vitamin deficiencies can also contribute.\n\n**Why Apple Cider Vinegar Sometimes Helps**\n- Apple cider vinegar (ACV) introduces mild acid, which can help restore proper stomach acidity and signal the LES to close, reducing reflux for some people.\n- However, if ACV worsens your symptoms, discontinue use.\n\n**Key Takeaway for You**\n- If you experience acid reflux, it may be due to insufficient stomach acid rather than excess. Addressing diet, stress, and meal timing can help. ACV is a common home remedy, but only if it relieves—not worsens—your symptoms.\n\nWould you like tips on how to naturally boost stomach acid or more guidance on safe remedies?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0023-27-00769:8": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0046-28-07406:3": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0030-73-19245:0": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0019-50-08651:6": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0030-73-19245:1": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I enjoy apple, kiwi, and watermelon.", "I want to change my lifestyle.", "I have gained weight recently because I stopped exercising for the last 6 months.", "I spent last summer in Brazil and since then love fresh ma