{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-2_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To help you shift toward a healthier, more active lifestyle—while factoring in your software engineer schedule, frequent dining out, and late-night dinners—here’s a practical, personalized action plan:\n\n**1. Smarter Meal Timing & Choices**\n- **Late Dinners:** If you can’t avoid eating late, opt for lighter meals (e.g., grilled fish/chicken with salad, veggie stir-fry). Heavy meals late at night disrupt sleep and metabolism.\n- **Meal Prep for Busy Nights:** Prepare simple, healthy dishes in advance (like soups or baked veggies) and refrigerate. This saves time and helps you avoid unhealthy takeout after long workdays.\n- **Split Your Dinner:** If you work out in the evening, eat the carb portion before exercise for energy, then have protein/veggies after.\n\n**2. Healthier Eating Out**\n- **Pack or Order Smart:** When eating out or ordering in, choose lean proteins (turkey, grilled chicken, fish), whole grains, and lots of vegetables. Avoid heavy, greasy, or high-sodium options.\n- **Snack Wisely:** Keep healthy snacks (almonds, fruit, yogurt) at your desk to avoid vending machine temptations.\n\n**3. Build Sustainable Habits**\n- **Meal Planning:** Spend 10 minutes weekly to plan easy, healthy meals. Make a list of go-to recipes you enjoy and can prepare quickly.\n- **Routine:** Try to eat at regular times to prevent overeating at night. If possible, shift your main meal earlier in the day.\n\n**4. Small Active Changes**\n- Walk or stretch during work breaks.\n- Consider biking or walking part of your commute.\n\nWould you like a sample weekly meal plan or quick recipe ideas tailored to your schedule?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0029-04-16046:11": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0028-10-01926:8": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0016-05-12651:4": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0023-54-04181:4": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0017-24-00677: