{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-2_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For combining yoga with swimming near London, here’s what you need to know about budget and options:\n\n**Top Outdoor Swimming Spots & Costs**\n\n- **West Reservoir Centre (Hackney)**\n  - Open-water swimming, urban setting.\n  - £10 per 50-minute session (book via Better UK app).\n\n- **Hampstead Heath Ponds**\n  - Iconic natural ponds, open early and late.\n  - £4 per swim for adults, £2.40 for concessions.\n  - No booking needed for many sessions.\n\n- **London Fields Lido (Hackney)**\n  - 50m heated outdoor pool, open year-round.\n  - £5.25 per swim (non-member), £3.70 (pay-and-play member).\n  - Monthly membership options available.\n\n- **Oasis Sports Centre (West End)**\n  - Heated outdoor and indoor pools.\n  - £6.15 per swim, or £35/month for access to 20+ pools.\n\n- **Beckenham Place Park Lake (Lewisham)**\n  - Open-water lake swimming.\n  - Induction required (£10), then pay per session.\n  - All swimmers must use a tow float.\n\n**Yoga**\n- Most leisure centres with pools also offer yoga classes.\n- Expect £8–£15 per class, or included in some memberships.\n\n**Personalized Guidance**\n- If you want flexibility and variety, a monthly membership (e.g., Better UK, £32–£35/month) gives access to multiple pools and often includes fitness classes like yoga.\n- For occasional swims, pay-as-you-go is cost-effective.\n\nWould you like help finding yoga classes at any of these locations, or tips on combining your swim and yoga sessions for best recovery?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0012-69-04768:1": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0041-93-14527:7": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0012-66-17212:0": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0012-69-04768:2": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0041-93-14527:2": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work at a desk job.", "I used to live in Edinburgh but moved to London last year.", "I am climbing regularly for the p