{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Combining yoga and open water swimming is an excellent choice—especially for someone with your climbing background and current recovery needs.\n\n**Why This Combo Works for You:**\n- **Physical Synergy:** Both yoga and swimming are low-impact, making them ideal while your finger heals. Swimming builds all-body strength and cardio without stressing joints; yoga enhances flexibility, mobility, and core stability—skills that directly benefit climbing.\n- **Injury Prevention & Recovery:** Yoga improves body awareness and mobility, which helps prevent overuse injuries common in repetitive sports like climbing and swimming. Swimming, especially in open water, supports circulation and gentle muscle engagement, aiding recovery.\n- **Mental Health Boost:** Both activities are proven to reduce stress and improve mood. Yoga’s focus on breath and mindfulness complements the meditative rhythm of swimming, helping combat the “blue” feeling you mentioned.\n- **Adaptability:** You can tailor both practices to your energy level and recovery status. For yoga, home-based routines (via apps or online classes) are effective and affordable. For swimming, open water offers a refreshing change of scenery and a sense of adventure.\n\n**Budget & Practical Tips:**\n- Yoga at home: Minimal cost (just a mat/app subscription).\n- Open water swimming: Initial gear investment (~£160), but low ongoing costs.\n\n**Personalized Note:** As a climber, you’ll likely appreciate how yoga’s mobility work and swimming’s endurance training can keep you fit and motivated, even off the wall.\n\nWould you like recommendations for specific yoga routines for swimmers, or tips on safe open water swimming as you recover?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0026-52-18893:0": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0026-52-18893:13": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0032-45-08030:1": 0.3333333333333