{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You’re planning for a 10km run in April, with a two-week vacation in January. Here’s how to keep your training on track and stress-free:\n\n**1. Flexibility Is Key**\n- It’s normal to adjust your plan for vacations. Consistency over months matters more than any single week.\n- If you know your vacation dates, treat that period as a “stepback” or recovery phase—intentionally reduce your training load to allow your body to rest and recharge (clueweb22-en0002-57-15129, clueweb22-en0007-93-18632).\n- If you can, fit in a few easy runs or cross-training sessions during your vacation, but don’t stress if you miss workouts. The overall pattern of training is what counts.\n\n**2. Adjusting Your Plan**\n- Before and after your vacation, maintain your regular schedule. If you miss key workouts, you can shift them earlier or later in the week (clueweb22-en0022-92-01169).\n- After vacation, resume your plan at a slightly reduced intensity for a few days to avoid injury, then ramp back up.\n\n**3. Motivation and Progress**\n- Taking a break can actually help prevent burnout and keep you motivated for the months ahead.\n- Use your vacation as a mental reset, then return focused for the final build-up to your race.\n\nWould you like a sample “stepback” week plan for your vacation, or tips on easy workouts you can do while traveling?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0042-72-11730:7": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0042-72-11730:6": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0022-92-01169:16": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0007-93-18632:11": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0002-57-15129:17": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0042-72-11730:7": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0042-72-11730:6": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0022-92-01169:16": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0007-93-18632:11": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0002-57-15129:17": 0.2, "clueweb22-en0007-93-18632:4": 0.16666666