{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For a healthier, low-carb, nutrient-rich lunch that supports your calcium needs, consider swapping white rice for these top alternatives:\n\n**Best Low-Carb, High-Nutrient Rice Alternatives**\n\n- **Cauliflower Rice**\n  - *Carbs*: ~5g per cup (vs. 45g+ in white rice)\n  - *Protein*: 2g per cup\n  - *Nutrients*: High in vitamin C, folate, vitamin K, and fiber\n  - *Calcium*: Modest, but higher than white rice\n  - *Why it fits*: Extremely low-carb, easy to prepare, and adds micronutrients missing from white rice.\n\n- **Broccoli Rice**\n  - *Carbs*: Similar to cauliflower rice, very low\n  - *Protein*: Slightly higher than cauliflower\n  - *Nutrients*: Good source of fiber, plant protein, iron, and some calcium\n  - *Why it fits*: Adds variety and more nutrients, especially if you want to rotate options.\n\n- **Quinoa**\n  - *Carbs*: Higher than cauliflower, but lower than white rice\n  - *Protein*: Complete protein, contains all essential amino acids\n  - *Nutrients*: Rich in magnesium, iron, and some calcium\n  - *Why it fits*: If you want more protein and nutrients, quinoa is a strong plant-based option.\n\n- **Seeds as Toppings**\n  - *Calcium boost*: Sprinkle chia, sesame, or poppy seeds on your rice alternative for a significant calcium increase.\n\n**What to Avoid**\n- White rice: High in carbs, low in protein, fiber, and calcium.\n\n**Personalized Recommendation**\nSwitch to cauliflower or broccoli rice for lunch, and top with calcium-rich seeds. This directly addresses your low-carb, high-nutrient, and calcium concerns.\n\nWould you like quick recipes or meal ideas using these ingredients?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0032-31-12698:0": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0007-64-04958:25": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0018-51-09385:1": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0007-64-04958:1": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0018-51-09385:0": 0.2