{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For a healthier lunch, here are the best rice alternatives, focusing on nutrient density, lower carbs, and fiber—ideal if you want to balance your meals, especially since you enjoy cake as a snack.\n\n**Top Rice Alternatives for Lunch**\n\n- **Cauliflower Rice**\n  - ~25 kcal/100g, 5g carbs, 2g fiber\n  - Very low in calories and carbs, high in vitamin C, K, and folate\n  - Mild flavor, easy to pair with most dishes\n\n- **Broccoli Rice**\n  - Similar calories and carbs to cauliflower rice\n  - Adds extra fiber, plant protein, and iron\n  - Subtle taste, works well in stir-fries and salads\n\n- **Shirataki Rice (Miracle Rice)**\n  - Virtually zero calories and carbs, high in soluble fiber\n  - Made from konjac root, gluten-free\n  - Neutral flavor, absorbs sauces well\n\n- **Sweet Potato Rice**\n  - ~110 kcal/100g, 23g carbs, 5g fiber\n  - Higher in carbs but rich in vitamin C and fiber\n  - Slightly sweet, good for variety\n\n- **Other Options**\n  - **Rutabaga Rice:** Low-carb, root vegetable, 9g net carbs/serving, 3.5g fiber\n  - **Butternut Squash Rice:** 13.6g net carbs/cup, high in vitamin A, C, E\n\n**Personalized Guidance**\n- Since you enjoy cake and juice, choosing low-carb, high-fiber lunch bases like cauliflower, broccoli, or shirataki rice helps balance your daily carb and calorie intake, leaving room for your preferred snacks.\n- These options are easy to prepare and versatile for different cuisines.\n\nWould you like quick recipes or ideas for pairing these rice alternatives with protein-rich or calcium-rich lunch options?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0032-31-12698:1": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0032-31-12698:0": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0018-51-09385:1": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0007-64-04958:25": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0036-70-04163:12": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I think I don't get enough calcium, a