{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Breastfeeding does not require a special or restrictive diet—your usual foods, including jam, white rice, cake, and orange juice, are all fine to continue enjoying.\n\n**Key Points for Your Diet While Breastfeeding:**\n\n- **No Need for Major Changes:** You can eat most foods you enjoyed before, including jam, rice, cake, and juice. There are no strict foods to avoid unless your baby shows a specific sensitivity (rare).\n- **Balanced Diet Matters:** Aim for a mix of fruits, vegetables, protein, dairy (or alternatives), and whole grains. This supports your energy and overall health, which helps you care for your baby.\n- **Carbs and Sweets:** White rice and cake are okay in moderation. Carbohydrates are important for energy, but if you’re interested in low-carb options, you can swap some white rice for whole grains or add more protein and veggies to meals.\n- **Jam and Orange Juice:** Both are safe. Jam is fine in typical amounts, and orange juice provides vitamin C and folate.\n- **Hydration:** Drink plenty of fluids—water and milk are especially good.\n- **Supplements:** Continuing a multivitamin with folic acid is recommended.\n\n**Foods to Limit:** Only a few things need moderation—alcohol (occasional, with caution), and very high amounts of caffeine.\n\n**Personalized Tip:** Since you bake cakes weekly and enjoy carbs, you don’t need to cut them out, but you can experiment with lower-sugar recipes or wholegrain flours if you want to try lower-carb baking.\n\nWould you like ideas for easy, nutritious snacks or tips on low-carb baking for breastfeeding?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0029-93-12021:2": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0042-99-06708:8": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0038-01-04875:10": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0011-53-14159:11": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0016-57-03787:2": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I eat jam for break