{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "After microneedling, your skin is temporarily more sensitive and permeable. To protect your results and avoid irritation—especially given your current routine with vitamin C, retinol, and AHA/BHA—here’s how to safely resume your skincare:\n\n**Immediate Aftercare (First 48–72 hours):**\n- **Cleanser:** Use only a gentle, fragrance-free cleanser (e.g., La Roche-Posay, Avene, or similar) after 8–24 hours. Avoid scrubs or cleansing brushes for at least a week.\n- **Moisturizer:** Stick to soothing, non-active moisturizers (e.g., La Roche-Posay Double Repair, Vichy Mineral 89, or a basic hyaluronic acid serum). Avoid actives like vitamin C, retinol, AHA/BHA, and highly fragranced products.\n- **Sunscreen:** Apply a physical (mineral) sunscreen before going outside, but only after the initial redness subsides (usually after several hours). Avoid sun exposure as much as possible.\n- **Makeup:** Do not apply makeup for at least 24–48 hours post-procedure.\n\n**When to Resume Your Routine:**\n- **Hyaluronic Acid:** You can resume gentle hyaluronic acid serums after 24 hours if your skin feels comfortable.\n- **Vitamin C, Retinol, AHA/BHA:** Wait at least 3–5 days, or until all redness and sensitivity have resolved, before reintroducing these actives. Start slowly and monitor for irritation.\n\n**Why This Matters for You:**\nYour current actives (vitamin C, retinol, AHA/BHA) can cause significant irritation if used too soon after microneedling. Prioritize barrier repair and hydration first.\n\nWould you like a sample post-microneedling routine tailored to your favorite La Roche-Posay products?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:6": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0008-38-11917:8": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:16": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:3": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0037-66-15379:13": 0.2}, "ptkb_pro