{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You asked if you can continue using your salicylic acid face wash after microneedling, given your oily skin and scalp.\n\n**Direct Answer:**  \nIt’s best to pause your salicylic acid face wash for at least 3 days after microneedling.\n\n**Key Points:**\n- **Why Pause?** Salicylic acid (a beta hydroxy acid) can irritate and dry out freshly microneedled skin, slowing healing and increasing sensitivity.\n- **When to Resume:** Wait at least 3 days post-treatment before reintroducing salicylic acid. Some sources recommend up to a week of gentle care, especially if your skin feels sensitive.\n- **What to Use Instead:** Stick to gentle, hydrating cleansers and moisturizers (look for fragrance-free, non-comedogenic formulas). Hyaluronic acid is ideal for hydration.\n- **Oily Skin Tip:** While you may feel oilier during this period, it’s important not to over-cleanse or use harsh products, as this can disrupt healing and worsen irritation.\n\n**Personalized Justification:**  \nBecause you have oily skin and rely on salicylic acid, it’s understandable to want to keep using it. However, protecting your skin’s barrier after microneedling will give you the best results and minimize complications.\n\n**Next Step:**  \nWould you like recommendations for gentle cleansers or moisturizers to use during your post-microneedling recovery?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:10": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0002-91-08989:13": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0030-56-13743:9": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0044-05-19112:9": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0000-59-08693:13": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I've noticed dark spots and uneven tone on my face.", "I apply Hyaluronic Acid two times a day after washing my face.", "I have visible pores on my cheeks and nose.", "I use AHA BHA serum once a week.", "I'm interested in treatments that improve my skin with 