{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_13", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Microneedling vs. Mesotherapy: Which Is Better for You?\n\nGiven your goals—fast improvement in skin appearance, minimal downtime, and suitability for oily skin—here’s how microneedling and mesotherapy compare:\n\n**Microneedling**\n- **How it works:** Creates micro-injuries in the skin to stimulate collagen, elastin, and hyaluronic acid production, leading to smoother, brighter skin.\n- **Best for:** Reducing acne scars, pores, fine lines, pigmentation, and dullness.\n- **Results:** Noticeable improvement after 2–3 weeks; optimal after several sessions.\n- **Downtime:** Minimal (redness for 1–2 days).\n- **Suitability:** Safe for oily skin; no risk of adding extra oil.\n- **Aftercare:** Avoid strong actives (like salicylic acid) for 3 days post-treatment.\n\n**Mesotherapy**\n- **How it works:** Injects a customized blend of vitamins, hyaluronic acid, antioxidants, and peptides directly into the skin’s middle layer.\n- **Best for:** Hydration, glow, mild plumping, targeting pigmentation, and early signs of aging.\n- **Results:** Some see a “glow” after one session; deeper issues (scarring, pigmentation) require multiple treatments.\n- **Downtime:** Minimal; usually no visible marks.\n- **Suitability:** Can be tailored for oily skin, but hydration effect may feel heavier if you’re prone to oiliness.\n- **Aftercare:** Similar to microneedling; gentle skincare recommended.\n\n**Key Differences**\n- **Microneedling** is better for texture, scars, and pores—ideal if you want visible smoothing and rejuvenation.\n- **Mesotherapy** excels at hydration and radiance, with customizable ingredients for specific concerns (e.g., pigmentation, early aging).\n\n**Recommendation:**  \nFor oily skin and a desire for fast, visible improvement in texture and clarity, microneedling is likely the better fit. Mesotherapy is a good add-on if you want extra hydration or targeted pigment correction.\n\nWould you like advice on choosing a clinic, or tips for combining these treatments safely?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0037-79-06507:2": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:1": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:6": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:2": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:5": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I've noticed dark spots and uneven tone on my face.", "I apply Hyaluronic Acid two times a day after washing my face.", "I have visible pores on my cheeks and nose.", "I use AHA BHA serum once a week.", "I'm interested in treatments that improve my skin with minimal downtime.", "I use vitamin C and Retinol every day in my morning routine.", "I usually wear makeup to even out my complexion."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0037-79-06507:2": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:1": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:6": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:2": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:5": 0.2, "clueweb22-en0020-68-08676:4": 0.16666666666666666, "clueweb22-en0014-30-12480:8": 0.14285714285714285, "clueweb22-en0019-24-02399:5": 0.125, "clueweb22-en0010-79-08092:8": 0.1111111111111111, "clueweb22-en0027-29-01748:10": 0.1, "clueweb22-en0012-49-09099:0": 0.09090909090909091, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:8": 0.08333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0005-98-19840:4": 0.07692307692307693, "clueweb22-en0000-96-07244:6": 0.07142857142857142, "clueweb22-en0017-69-06314:0": 0.06666666666666667, "clueweb22-en0005-52-08775:1": 0.0625, "clueweb22-en0005-52-08775:0": 0.058823529411764705, "clueweb22-en0009-67-17389:4": 0.05555555555555555, "clueweb22-en0000-96-07244:7": 0.05263157894736842, "clueweb22-en0026-30-09048:10": 0.05, "clueweb22-en0010-79-08092:9": 0.047619047619047616, "clueweb22-en0007-65-12324:7": 0.045454545454545456, "clueweb22-en0016-80-15701:7": 0.043478260869565216, "clueweb22-en0044-86-11559:2": 0.041666666666666664, "clueweb22-en0014-79-13828:0": 0.04, "clueweb22-en0021-0