{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-2_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To find the best shampoo for your hair, focus on these essentials:\n\n**1. Identify Your Hair Type**\n- **Dry Hair:** Look for shampoos labeled as moisturizing, nourishing, or hydrating. Ingredients like natural oils and butters are beneficial.\n- **Thin/Fine Hair:** Choose volumizing or thickening shampoos. Avoid heavy conditioners that can weigh hair down.\n- **Color-Treated Hair:** Select shampoos marked as color-safe or color-protecting to prevent fading.\n- **Damaged Hair:** Opt for strengthening, repairing, or anti-breakage formulas with fortifying ingredients.\n- **Oily Hair:** Consider clarifying shampoos with robust cleansing agents.\n\n**2. Prioritize Quality Ingredients**\n- Natural ingredients (e.g., essential oils, avocado oil, green tea) are generally better for hair health.\n- Avoid shampoos with harsh chemicals, especially if your hair is sensitive or treated.\n\n**3. Invest in Quality**\n- Cheap shampoos often contain low-quality ingredients that can damage hair. Salon-quality or reputable natural brands (like Acure, Rahua, John Masters, Shea Moisture) are worth the investment.\n\n**4. Personalization**\n- What works for someone else may not work for you. Be open to trying a few options tailored to your specific needs.\n\nWould you like recommendations for specific brands or help narrowing down options based on your hair type?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0017-18-05896:1": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0036-03-13080:12": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0001-81-10587:4": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0035-29-17417:4": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0045-30-03373:4": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I'm allergic to nuts, so I have to be careful about ingredients.", "I frequently use heat styling tools to keep my hair looking good.", "I'm thinking about getting a new haircut soon."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0017-18-05896:1": 1