{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-2_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For oily hair, ingredient selection is crucial. Here’s what to look for—and what to avoid—based on your needs:\n\n**Best Ingredients for Oily Hair**\n- **Detergents for Oil Control:** Shampoos containing sodium lauryl sulfate, ammonium lauryl sulfate, or sulfosuccinates are effective at removing excess oil from the scalp. These are strong cleansers that help keep oil at bay.\n- **Volumizing/Balancing Formulas:** Choose shampoos labeled “volumizing,” “strengthening,” or “balancing.” These are specifically formulated to manage oil without weighing hair down.\n\n**Ingredients to Avoid**\n- **Heavy Moisturizers:** Avoid shampoos labeled “moisturizing,” “hydrating,” or “smoothing,” as well as those for curly or frizzy hair. These often contain oils and emollients that can make oily hair feel greasy.\n- **Oils and Rich Conditioners:** Steer clear of products with added oils (like argan, coconut, or jojoba) unless your hair is also dry at the ends.\n- **Harsh Chemicals:** If you prefer a gentler approach, avoid parabens, phthalates, and strong sulfates, as these can irritate the scalp or strip too much natural oil, potentially triggering more oil production.\n\n**Natural Alternatives**\n- If you want a more natural formula, look for shampoos with minimal, plant-derived ingredients and no synthetic fragrances or preservatives.\n\n**Pro Tip:** Use clarifying shampoos occasionally for deep cleansing, but not daily, to prevent over-drying.\n\nWould you like specific product recommendations or tips on how often to wash for best results?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0018-54-01822:10": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0014-71-05022:3": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0037-41-10440:4": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0029-89-12181:3": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0026-19-17834:1": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I'm allergic to nuts, so I have to be careful about