{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-2_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For your oily scalp and frequent heat styling, the best shampoo will balance oil control with scalp health and protection against heat-related damage.\n\n**Key Ingredients to Look For:**\n- **Niacinamide:** Supports scalp barrier, reduces oiliness, and soothes irritation—ideal for oily, sensitive scalps.\n- **Lactic Acid (or LHA):** Gently exfoliates, unclogs pores, and helps regulate oil without over-drying.\n- **Salicylic Acid:** Deeply cleanses and breaks down excess oil and buildup.\n- **Panthenol & Hydrolyzed Keratin:** Strengthen hair, reduce breakage, and help repair heat damage.\n- **Zinc Pyrithione:** Controls dandruff and scalp irritation, often linked to excess oil.\n- **Natural Extracts (e.g., sage, tea tree, licorice root):** Refresh scalp, provide mild antimicrobial action, and help maintain oil balance.\n\n**Formulation Tips for Heat-Styled Hair:**\n- Avoid harsh, overly stripping shampoos (e.g., those with only strong sulfates) as they can make hair brittle after heat styling.\n- Look for formulas free from silicones, parabens, and synthetic fragrances to minimize buildup and irritation.\n- Shampoos with a pH around 5.5 are gentle and scalp-compatible.\n\n**Routine Enhancements:**\n- Use a clarifying shampoo only occasionally to prevent over-drying.\n- Minimize touching your hair to reduce oil transfer.\n- Consider a lightweight, leave-in heat protectant after washing.\n\n**Top Recommendation:**  \nA shampoo containing niacinamide, lactic acid or LHA, panthenol, and natural extracts (like licorice root or tea tree) will best address your needs—balancing oil, soothing the scalp, and supporting hair resilience against heat.\n\nWould you like specific product recommendations that match these criteria?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0029-13-07561:5": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0018-54-01822:9": 0.5, "clue