{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-2_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Here’s a direct price and feature comparison for the three shampoos you asked about—OUAI Detox Shampoo, Head & Shoulders Instant Oil Control, and La Roche-Posay Kerium DS—tailored for your oily scalp and oily hair needs:\n\n**OUAI Detox Shampoo**\n- **Price:** $30 for 10 oz ($3.00/oz)\n- **Key Features:** Sulphate-free, clarifies with apple cider vinegar, removes oil and buildup, strengthens with keratin, pleasant rose scent.\n- **Best for:** Deep cleansing once a week, especially if you use styling products or want a more natural formula.\n\n**Head & Shoulders Instant Oil Control Anti-Dandruff Shampoo**\n- **Price:** Typically ranges from $6–$10 for a standard bottle (exact size and price may vary by retailer).\n- **Key Features:** Targets oil and dandruff from first wash, contains mango and citrus extracts, 3-Action Formula for cleansing, protection, and light moisturization.\n- **Best for:** Frequent use to control both oil and flakes, budget-friendly.\n\n**La Roche-Posay Kerium DS Anti-Dandruff Intensive Shampoo**\n- **Price:** $21.39 for 125ml (~4.2 oz), or about $12 for a 400ml bottle (pricing varies by retailer and region).\n- **Key Features:** Intensive treatment for oily dandruff, contains LHA for micro-exfoliation, niacinamide (Vitamin PP) for soothing, gel-cream texture, paraben-free.\n- **Best for:** Twice-weekly use for oily scalp with persistent dandruff and itching.\n\n**Summary:**  \n- OUAI is the most expensive, ideal for deep, occasional detox.\n- Head & Shoulders is the most affordable and practical for regular use.\n- La Roche-Posay is a mid-range, targeted treatment for oily dandruff.\n\nWould you like advice on how to rotate these shampoos for best results, or links to where you can buy them at the best price?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0043-27-07235:0": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0031-38-06