{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned-rankllm", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "7-1_13", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You already have a scale and measuring cups, which covers the essentials for accurate bread baking. To further improve your results and make the process easier, consider adding these tools:\n\n**Must-Have for Oven Bread:**\n- **Oven Thermometer:** Ensures your oven is at the correct temperature, which is crucial for consistent bread texture and rise.\n- **Large Mixing Bowl:** Gives you space to mix and knead dough comfortably.\n- **Bread Thermometer (Instant-Read):** Lets you check if your bread is fully baked (ideal internal temp: 190–210°F).\n\n**Highly Recommended for Better Results:**\n- **Dutch Oven or Baking Stone:** Both help create a crisp crust and even bake. A Dutch oven traps steam for a professional finish; a baking stone gives great bottom heat.\n- **Bench/Dough Scraper:** Makes handling and shaping dough easier and cleaner.\n- **Cooling Rack:** Prevents soggy bottoms by allowing air to circulate around your bread as it cools.\n- **Bread Lame (Scoring Tool):** For slashing dough before baking, which controls expansion and improves appearance.\n\n**Why These?**\n- These tools directly support healthy, whole-grain bread baking at home, which aligns with your focus on liver health and ingredient control.\n- They’re all reusable and don’t require a big investment.\n\nWould you like quick tips on using any of these tools, or a simple healthy bread recipe to get started?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0046-36-14913:3": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0034-06-02443:13": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0039-87-01606:2": 0.3333333333333333, "clueweb22-en0022-71-14456:4": 0.25, "clueweb22-en0033-05-06665:2": 0.2}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I like to challenge myself.", "I have some basic baking experience.", "I enjoy baking."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0046-36-14913:3": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0034-06-02443:13": 0.5, "clueweb22-en0039-87